                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+deformation+quantization"} strict deformation quantization
          %h2#references References
          %p The “path method” of integrating Lie algebras to simply connected Lie groups appears in
          %ul
            %li#DuistermaatKolk00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans+Duistermaat"}> Hans Duistermaat
              , J. A. C. Kolk, section 1.14 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie groups
          %p
            The idea of identifying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+construction"} Sullivan construction
            applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            as Lie integration to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
          %ul
            %li#Hinich97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Descent of Deligne groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1155/S1073792897000160"} doi
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.haifa.ac.il/hinich/WEB/mypapers/ddg.pdf"} preprint ddg.pdf
          %p
            and for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+L-infinity+algebras"} nilpotent L-infinity algebras
          %ul
            %li#Getzler04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ezra+Getzler"}> Ezra Getzler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Lie theory for nilpotent
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  algebras
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404003"} math.AT/0404003
          %p
            whose main point is the discussion of a gauge condition applicable for nilpotent
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Robert-Nicoud"}> Daniel Robert-Nicoud
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Vallette"} Bruno Vallette
              %em Higher Lie theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.10485"}> arXiv:2010.10485
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            with generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curved+L-infinity+algebras"}
              curved
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Roca+i+Lucio"}> Victor Roca i Lucio
              \:
              %em
                The integration theory of curved absolute
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_\infty
                algebras
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.10282"}> arXiv:2209.10282
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and generalized to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+characteristic"} positive characteristic
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Roca+i+Lucio"}> Victor Roca i Lucio
              \:
              %em Higher Lie theory in positive characteristic
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.07829"}> arXiv:2306.07829
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            This Lie integration is refined from taking values in bare
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %span.newWikiWord
              internal ∞-groupoids
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/internal+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ?
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+manifolds"} Banach manifolds
            by
          %ul
            %li#Henriques
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Integrating
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  algebras
              %strong 144
              (2008), no. 4, 1017–1045 (
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1112/S0010437X07003405"}> doi
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0603563"}> math.AT/0603563
              )
          %p (whose origin possibly preceeds that of Getzler’s article).
          %p
            For general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroids"} ∞-Lie algebroids
            the general idea of the integration process by “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            \-paths” had been indicated in
          %ul
            %li#Severa01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+Severa"}> Pavol Severa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+title+containing+the+words+%22homotopy%22+and+%22symplectic%22%2C+e.g.+this+one"} Some title containing the words "homotopy" and "symplectic", e.g. this one
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.lpthe.jussieu.fr/~dito/poissongeometry/Poisson2000/index.html"} Poisson 2000
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cirm-math.fr/"} CIRM Marseille Luminy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105080"} arXiv:0105080
            %li
              %p
                Pavol Ševera, Michal Širaň,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Integration of differential graded manifolds
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.04898"} arxiv/1506.04898
          %p
            Cast along the lines of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie%27s+third+theorem"} Lie's third theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+L.+Rogers"}> Christopher L. Rogers
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesse+Wolfson"} Jesse Wolfson
              %em
                Lie’s Third Theorem for Lie
                = succeed "-Algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08957"}> arXiv:2409.08957
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Lie integration of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spectrum"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+spectra"} parameterized spectra
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+theories"} differential cohomology theories
          %ul
            %li#BraunackMayer18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Braunack-Mayer"}> Vincent Braunack-Mayer
              , section 3.1 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/thesis+Braunack-Mayer"} Rational parameterized stable homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/thesis+Braunack-Mayer#pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of Lie integration of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
            by the path method is due to
          %ul
            %li#Crainic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"}> Marius Crainic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rui+Loja+Fernandes"} Rui Loja Fernandes
              = succeed "," do
                %em Integrability of Lie brackets
              %strong 157
              2 (2003) 575-620 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.DG/0105033"}> arXiv:math.DG/0105033
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2003.157.575"} doi:10.4007/annals.2003.157.575
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rui+Loja+Fernandes"}> Rui Loja Fernandes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"} Marius Crainic
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on Integrability of Lie Brackets
              %strong 17
              (2011) 1–107 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611259"}> arxiv:math.DG/0611259
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/gtm.2011.17.1"} doi:10.2140/gtm.2011.17.1
          %p
            and following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DuistermaatKolk00"} Duistermaat-Kolk (2000 section 1.14)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroids"} Poisson Lie algebroids
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoids"} symplectic groupoids
            in
          %ul
            %li#CattaneoFelder01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
              = succeed "," do
                %em Poisson sigma models and symplectic groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Singular Symplectic Quotients
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              %p
                2001), 61–93. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003023"}> arXiv:math/0003023
                )
          %p upgraded to the stacky version by
          %ul
            %li#TZ
              Tseng Hsiang-Hua,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Integrating Lie algebroids via stacks
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0405003"} arXiv:math/0405003
          %p
            A general proof that equivalent
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Rogers"}> Christopher Rogers
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              %em On the homotopy theory for Lie ∞-groupoids, with an application to integrating L∞-algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.01394"}> arXiv:1609.01394
              )
          %p Obstruction interpreted as transgression of a Lie algebroid fibration by
          %ul
            %li#BZ
              Olivier Brahic,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie algebroid fibrations
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.4904"} arXiv:1001.4904
          %p
            A description of Lie integration with values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            (and further the Lie integration of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} L-infinity cocycles
          %ul
            %li#FSS12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+Cocycles+for+Differential+characteristic+Classes"} Cech Cocycles for Differential characteristic Classes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4735"} arXiv:1011.4735
          %p Essentially the same integration prescription is considered in
          %ul
            %li#Roytenberg09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
              ,
              %em Differential graded manifolds and associated stacks: an overview
              (
              %a{:href => "https://sites.google.com/site/dmitryroytenberg/unpublished/dg-stacks-overview.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The Lie integration- of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-algebroid+representation"} Lie algebroid representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo →
                  %mi end
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} \to end(V)
            to morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-categories"} ∞-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to Ch_\bullet^\circ
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Camilo+Arias+Abad"}> Camilo Arias Abad
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Florian+Sch%C3%A4tz"} Florian Schätz
              %em
                The
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
                de Rham theorem and integration of representations up to homotopy
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4693"}> arXiv:1011.4693
              )
          %p Application to the problem of Lie integrating ordinary but infinite-dimensional Lie algebras is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Wockel"}> Christoph Wockel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              %em Integrating central extensions of Lie algebras via Lie 2-groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1204.5583"}> arXiv:1204.5583
              )
          %p
            A generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            to conjectural Leibniz groups has been conjectured by
            = succeed "." do
